{
  "info": {
    "name": "Face Attendance API",
    "_postman_id": "fa5e0000-0000-4000-8000-face00000001",
    "description": "Three-pose face registration and attendance verification.\n\n## Before you start\n\n1. Run the API: `dotnet run --project src/Api` (or F5 in VS Code).\n2. Run **1. Health and diagnostics > Which engine is live** first. If providerId starts with `development:` then NO real face recognition is happening - the stub matches on upload FILE NAME, so alice-front.jpg, alice-left.jpg and alice-right.jpg enrol as one person and bob-*.jpg will not match them. That is the default so the front end can be built before the models exist.\n3. Run **2. Registration > Register person + 3 poses**. It saves `personId` into a collection variable, so every request below it just works.\n\n## File uploads\n\nRequests with images point at `E:/FaceAttendance/docs/samples`. Postman may drop file paths on import for security - if a request says no file is selected, click the body row and pick the file again.\n\n## Keys\n\n`adminKey` can do everything. `deviceKey` can ONLY mark attendance - it cannot enrol a face or download a photograph, because it is the key most likely to be lifted off a kiosk.\n\n## Reading the responses\n\nA failed face match returns **200 with `success: false`** and a `decision` code - the request was valid, it simply did not match. 4xx is reserved for malformed requests. Errors are RFC 9457 problem documents with a stable `code` field; branch on `code`, never on the prose in `detail`.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "1. Health and diagnostics",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Health (no API key needed)",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "X-Tenant-Id",
                "value": "{{tenantId}}"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/health",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "health"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Liveness, including a database check. The only endpoint that needs no key."
          },
          "response": [],
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "Which engine is live",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "X-Api-Key",
                "value": "{{adminKey}}"
              },
              {
                "key": "X-Tenant-Id",
                "value": "{{tenantId}}"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/v1/diagnostics/provider",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "v1",
                "diagnostics",
                "provider"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Run this FIRST. If providerId starts with 'development:' then no real face recognition is happening - it matches on upload file name. Also reports the thresholds every decision is made against."
          },
          "response": [],
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "const d = pm.response.json();",
                  "console.log('provider:', d.providerId);",
                  "pm.test('three poses required', () => pm.expect(d.requiredPoses.length).to.eql(3));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "Analyze a frame (stores nothing)",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "X-Api-Key",
                "value": "{{adminKey}}"
              },
              {
                "key": "X-Tenant-Id",
                "value": "{{tenantId}}"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/v1/diagnostics/analyze",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "v1",
                "diagnostics",
                "analyze"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Detection and quality scoring without storing anything. Use it to check camera placement and lighting before rolling out a kiosk.",
            "body": {
              "mode": "formdata",
              "formdata": [
                {
                  "key": "image",
                  "type": "file",
                  "src": "E:/FaceAttendance/docs/samples/alice-front.jpg"
                }
              ]
            }
          },
          "response": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "2. Registration",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Register person + 3 poses (ONE CALL)",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "X-Api-Key",
                "value": "{{adminKey}}"
              },
              {
                "key": "X-Tenant-Id",
                "value": "{{tenantId}}"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/v1/registrations",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "v1",
                "registrations"
              ]
            },
            "description": "The endpoint a capture wizard should use. Creates the person and stores all three angles together. If any image is rejected the person record is rolled back, so you never get a row that occupies the employee id but holds no usable face.\n\nSaves personId into a collection variable for the requests below.",
            "body": {
              "mode": "formdata",
              "formdata": [
                {
                  "key": "externalId",
                  "type": "text",
                  "value": "{{externalId}}",
                  "description": "Your own id: employee code, roll number"
                },
                {
                  "key": "fullName",
                  "type": "text",
                  "value": "Alice Kumar",
                  "description": ""
                },
                {
                  "key": "department",
                  "type": "text",
                  "value": "Operations",
                  "description": ""
                },
                {
                  "key": "front",
                  "type": "file",
                  "src": "E:/FaceAttendance/docs/samples/alice-front.jpg"
                },
                {
                  "key": "left",
                  "type": "file",
                  "src": "E:/FaceAttendance/docs/samples/alice-left.jpg"
                },
                {
                  "key": "right",
                  "type": "file",
                  "src": "E:/FaceAttendance/docs/samples/alice-right.jpg"
                }
              ]
            }
          },
          "response": [],
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('201 Created', () => pm.response.to.have.status(201));",
                  "const d = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set('personId', d.person.id);",
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set('externalId', d.person.externalId);",
                  "console.log('personId saved:', d.person.id, '| status:', d.enrollmentStatus);",
                  "pm.test('enrolled', () => pm.expect(d.enrollmentStatus).to.eql('Enrolled'));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "Create person only (no faces yet)",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "X-Api-Key",
                "value": "{{adminKey}}"
              },
              {
                "key": "X-Tenant-Id",
                "value": "{{tenantId}}"
              },
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/v1/persons",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "v1",
                "persons"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Step-by-step alternative: create the person, then post each pose separately so the capture screen can give feedback per angle.",
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"externalId\": \"EMP-3001\",\n  \"fullName\": \"Bob Singh\",\n  \"email\": \"bob@example.com\",\n  \"department\": \"Maintenance\"\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "response": [],
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "if (pm.response.code === 201) {",
                  "  pm.collectionVariables.set('stepPersonId', pm.response.json().id);",
                  "  console.log('stepPersonId saved');",
                  "} else { console.log('already exists:', pm.response.code); }"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "Add ONE pose",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "X-Api-Key",
                "value": "{{adminKey}}"
              },
              {
                "key": "X-Tenant-Id",
                "value": "{{tenantId}}"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/v1/persons/{{stepPersonId}}/faces",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "v1",
                "persons",
                "{{stepPersonId}}",
                "faces"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Store a single pose. Safe to repeat: a second capture of the same pose supersedes the first rather than duplicating it, so a retry always works.\n\nChange the pose field to Front, Left or Right.",
            "body": {
              "mode": "formdata",
              "formdata": [
                {
                  "key": "pose",
                  "type": "text",
                  "value": "Front",
                  "description": "Front | Left | Right"
                },
                {
                  "key": "image",
                  "type": "file",
                  "src": "E:/FaceAttendance/docs/samples/bob-front.jpg"
                }
              ]
            }
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "Add all 3 poses to an existing person",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "X-Api-Key",
                "value": "{{adminKey}}"
              },
              {
                "key": "X-Tenant-Id",
                "value": "{{tenantId}}"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/v1/persons/{{stepPersonId}}/faces/batch",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "v1",
                "persons",
                "{{stepPersonId}}",
                "faces",
                "batch"
              ]
            },
            "description": "All three angles for a person who already exists.",
            "body": {
              "mode": "formdata",
              "formdata": [
                {
                  "key": "front",
                  "type": "file",
                  "src": "E:/FaceAttendance/docs/samples/bob-front.jpg"
                },
                {
                  "key": "left",
                  "type": "file",
                  "src": "E:/FaceAttendance/docs/samples/bob-left.jpg"
                },
                {
                  "key": "right",
                  "type": "file",
                  "src": "E:/FaceAttendance/docs/samples/bob-right.jpg"
                }
              ]
            }
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "Enrollment status",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "X-Api-Key",
                "value": "{{adminKey}}"
              },
              {
                "key": "X-Tenant-Id",
                "value": "{{tenantId}}"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/v1/persons/{{personId}}/enrollment",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "v1",
                "persons",
                "{{personId}}",
                "enrollment"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Which poses are held, which are missing, and how similar the stored poses are to each other. providerMatchesCurrent tells you whether a template still belongs to the active engine - false means it needs re-capturing."
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "Get person by id",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "X-Api-Key",
                "value": "{{adminKey}}"
              },
              {
                "key": "X-Tenant-Id",
                "value": "{{tenantId}}"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/v1/persons/{{personId}}",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "v1",
                "persons",
                "{{personId}}"
              ]
            },
            "description": "One person."
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "Find by your own id",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "X-Api-Key",
                "value": "{{adminKey}}"
              },
              {
                "key": "X-Tenant-Id",
                "value": "{{tenantId}}"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/v1/persons/by-external-id/{{externalId}}",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "v1",
                "persons",
                "by-external-id",
                "{{externalId}}"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Look a person up by employee code rather than GUID."
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "Search people",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "X-Api-Key",
                "value": "{{adminKey}}"
              },
              {
                "key": "X-Tenant-Id",
                "value": "{{tenantId}}"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/v1/persons?query=alice&enrollmentStatus=Enrolled&page=1&pageSize=25",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "v1",
                "persons"
              ],
              "query": [
                {
                  "key": "query",
                  "value": "alice"
                },
                {
                  "key": "enrollmentStatus",
                  "value": "Enrolled"
                },
                {
                  "key": "page",
                  "value": "1"
                },
                {
                  "key": "pageSize",
                  "value": "25"
                }
              ]
            },
            "description": "Paged search. enrollmentStatus accepts NotEnrolled, InProgress, Enrolled or Stale."
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "Download a stored capture",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "X-Api-Key",
                "value": "{{adminKey}}"
              },
              {
                "key": "X-Tenant-Id",
                "value": "{{tenantId}}"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/v1/persons/{{personId}}/faces/Front/image",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "v1",
                "persons",
                "{{personId}}",
                "faces",
                "Front",
                "image"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Returns the stored JPEG. Admin only and deliberately not cacheable - it is a photograph of a person."
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "Delete one pose",
          "request": {
            "method": "DELETE",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "X-Api-Key",
                "value": "{{adminKey}}"
              },
              {
                "key": "X-Tenant-Id",
                "value": "{{tenantId}}"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/v1/persons/{{personId}}/faces/Left",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "v1",
                "persons",
                "{{personId}}",
                "faces",
                "Left"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Retires one angle. The person drops out of Enrolled until it is re-captured."
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "ERASE all biometrics",
          "request": {
            "method": "DELETE",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "X-Api-Key",
                "value": "{{adminKey}}"
              },
              {
                "key": "X-Tenant-Id",
                "value": "{{tenantId}}"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/v1/persons/{{personId}}/biometrics",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "v1",
                "persons",
                "{{personId}}",
                "biometrics"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Deletes every template and stored image for this person, including from the cloud provider when one is in use. This is the endpoint a data-erasure request needs.\n\nThe person record itself survives; only the biometric data goes."
          },
          "response": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "3. Attendance",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Mark attendance 1:1 (PREFERRED)",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "X-Api-Key",
                "value": "{{deviceKey}}"
              },
              {
                "key": "X-Tenant-Id",
                "value": "{{tenantId}}"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/v1/attendance/mark",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "v1",
                "attendance",
                "mark"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Send externalId or personId whenever the device can obtain it - a badge tap, a PIN, a name picker. The face then only has to CONFIRM the claim, and accuracy does not degrade as headcount grows.\n\nUses the DEVICE key, which can do nothing else.\n\nA non-match returns 200 with success:false and a decision code. Switch on decision, not on HTTP status.",
            "body": {
              "mode": "formdata",
              "formdata": [
                {
                  "key": "externalId",
                  "type": "text",
                  "value": "{{externalId}}",
                  "description": "Omit this to force a 1:N search"
                },
                {
                  "key": "deviceId",
                  "type": "text",
                  "value": "GATE-A",
                  "description": ""
                },
                {
                  "key": "image",
                  "type": "file",
                  "src": "E:/FaceAttendance/docs/samples/alice-front.jpg"
                }
              ]
            }
          },
          "response": [],
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('200 - a non-match is still 200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "const d = pm.response.json();",
                  "console.log(d.decision, '| score', d.score, 'vs threshold', d.threshold,",
                  "            '|', d.fullName || '(no match)', '|', d.direction || '');"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "Mark attendance 1:N (no id given)",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "X-Api-Key",
                "value": "{{deviceKey}}"
              },
              {
                "key": "X-Tenant-Id",
                "value": "{{tenantId}}"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/v1/attendance/mark",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "v1",
                "attendance",
                "mark"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Identification across the whole tenant. Convenient, but the false-accept rate rises with the number of enrolled people, so the threshold is stricter and a near-tie between two candidates is refused rather than guessed.",
            "body": {
              "mode": "formdata",
              "formdata": [
                {
                  "key": "deviceId",
                  "type": "text",
                  "value": "GATE-B",
                  "description": ""
                },
                {
                  "key": "image",
                  "type": "file",
                  "src": "E:/FaceAttendance/docs/samples/bob-front.jpg"
                }
              ]
            }
          },
          "response": [],
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('200 - a non-match is still 200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "const d = pm.response.json();",
                  "console.log(d.decision, '| score', d.score, 'vs threshold', d.threshold,",
                  "            '|', d.fullName || '(no match)', '|', d.direction || '');"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "Mark attendance with everything",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "X-Api-Key",
                "value": "{{deviceKey}}"
              },
              {
                "key": "X-Tenant-Id",
                "value": "{{tenantId}}"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/v1/attendance/mark",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "v1",
                "attendance",
                "mark"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Every field the endpoint accepts. direction is optional - leave it out and the server infers In or Out from the previous event, so a mis-tapped button cannot corrupt the day. capturedAtUtc is recorded but never trusted for ordering.",
            "body": {
              "mode": "formdata",
              "formdata": [
                {
                  "key": "externalId",
                  "type": "text",
                  "value": "{{externalId}}",
                  "description": ""
                },
                {
                  "key": "direction",
                  "type": "text",
                  "value": "In",
                  "description": "In | Out. Omit to let the server infer it"
                },
                {
                  "key": "deviceId",
                  "type": "text",
                  "value": "GATE-A",
                  "description": ""
                },
                {
                  "key": "latitude",
                  "type": "text",
                  "value": "19.0760",
                  "description": ""
                },
                {
                  "key": "longitude",
                  "type": "text",
                  "value": "72.8777",
                  "description": ""
                },
                {
                  "key": "capturedAtUtc",
                  "type": "text",
                  "value": "2026-10-09T09:00:00Z",
                  "description": ""
                },
                {
                  "key": "image",
                  "type": "file",
                  "src": "E:/FaceAttendance/docs/samples/alice-front.jpg"
                }
              ]
            }
          },
          "response": [],
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('200 - a non-match is still 200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "const d = pm.response.json();",
                  "console.log(d.decision, '| score', d.score, 'vs threshold', d.threshold,",
                  "            '|', d.fullName || '(no match)', '|', d.direction || '');"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "Preview a match (records NOTHING)",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "X-Api-Key",
                "value": "{{adminKey}}"
              },
              {
                "key": "X-Tenant-Id",
                "value": "{{tenantId}}"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/v1/attendance/preview",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "v1",
                "attendance",
                "preview"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Scores a frame without writing an attendance row. Use it for a live 'ready to punch' indicator, and to gather real score distributions from your own cameras before settling on a threshold.\n\nAdd a personId form field to score against one person instead of everybody.",
            "body": {
              "mode": "formdata",
              "formdata": [
                {
                  "key": "image",
                  "type": "file",
                  "src": "E:/FaceAttendance/docs/samples/alice-front.jpg"
                }
              ]
            }
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "Attendance register",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "X-Api-Key",
                "value": "{{adminKey}}"
              },
              {
                "key": "X-Tenant-Id",
                "value": "{{tenantId}}"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/v1/attendance?page=1&pageSize=50",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "v1",
                "attendance"
              ],
              "query": [
                {
                  "key": "page",
                  "value": "1"
                },
                {
                  "key": "pageSize",
                  "value": "50"
                }
              ]
            },
            "description": "Every attempt, accepted or not. The rejections are the audit trail you need when somebody says the machine did not recognise them."
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "Register for one person and date range",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "X-Api-Key",
                "value": "{{adminKey}}"
              },
              {
                "key": "X-Tenant-Id",
                "value": "{{tenantId}}"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/v1/attendance?personId={{personId}}&fromUtc=2026-10-09T00:00:00Z&toUtc=2026-10-10T00:00:00Z&pageSize=50",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "v1",
                "attendance"
              ],
              "query": [
                {
                  "key": "personId",
                  "value": "{{personId}}"
                },
                {
                  "key": "fromUtc",
                  "value": "2026-10-09T00:00:00Z"
                },
                {
                  "key": "toUtc",
                  "value": "2026-10-10T00:00:00Z"
                },
                {
                  "key": "decision",
                  "value": "Accepted",
                  "disabled": true
                },
                {
                  "key": "pageSize",
                  "value": "50"
                }
              ]
            },
            "description": "decision accepts Accepted, Rejected, Duplicate, NotEnrolled, NoFaceDetected, LowQuality, SpoofSuspected or ProviderError."
          },
          "response": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "4. These SHOULD fail",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "No API key",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "X-Tenant-Id",
                "value": "{{tenantId}}"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/v1/persons",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "v1",
                "persons"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Expect 401. Every endpoint except /health requires a key."
          },
          "response": [],
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('401 - unauthorized', () => pm.response.to.have.status(401));",
                  "console.log(pm.response.code, pm.response.text().slice(0, 200));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "Device key cannot enrol",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "X-Api-Key",
                "value": "{{deviceKey}}"
              },
              {
                "key": "X-Tenant-Id",
                "value": "{{tenantId}}"
              },
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/v1/persons",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "v1",
                "persons"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Expect 403. A device key can mark attendance and nothing else - it is the key most likely to be lifted off a kiosk, so it must not be able to enrol a face or read a stored photograph.",
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"externalId\": \"SHOULD-FAIL\",\n  \"fullName\": \"Nope\"\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "response": [],
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('403 - forbidden', () => pm.response.to.have.status(403));",
                  "console.log(pm.response.code, pm.response.text().slice(0, 200));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "Duplicate employee id",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "X-Api-Key",
                "value": "{{adminKey}}"
              },
              {
                "key": "X-Tenant-Id",
                "value": "{{tenantId}}"
              },
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/v1/persons",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "v1",
                "persons"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Expect 409 external_id_exists. Run the registration request first.",
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"externalId\": \"{{externalId}}\",\n  \"fullName\": \"Clash\"\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "response": [],
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('409 - conflict', () => pm.response.to.have.status(409));",
                  "console.log(pm.response.code, pm.response.text().slice(0, 200));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "Same face, different employee id",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "X-Api-Key",
                "value": "{{adminKey}}"
              },
              {
                "key": "X-Tenant-Id",
                "value": "{{tenantId}}"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/v1/registrations",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "v1",
                "registrations"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Expect 409 duplicate_identity. This is the guard that stops one person holding two identities and covering for an absent colleague. The new person record is rolled back, so no orphan row is left behind.",
            "body": {
              "mode": "formdata",
              "formdata": [
                {
                  "key": "externalId",
                  "type": "text",
                  "value": "FRAUD-9999",
                  "description": ""
                },
                {
                  "key": "fullName",
                  "type": "text",
                  "value": "Carol Impostor",
                  "description": ""
                },
                {
                  "key": "front",
                  "type": "file",
                  "src": "E:/FaceAttendance/docs/samples/alice-front.jpg"
                },
                {
                  "key": "left",
                  "type": "file",
                  "src": "E:/FaceAttendance/docs/samples/alice-left.jpg"
                },
                {
                  "key": "right",
                  "type": "file",
                  "src": "E:/FaceAttendance/docs/samples/alice-right.jpg"
                }
              ]
            }
          },
          "response": [],
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('409 - duplicate identity', () => pm.response.to.have.status(409));",
                  "console.log(pm.response.code, pm.response.text().slice(0, 200));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "Same frame for two poses",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "X-Api-Key",
                "value": "{{adminKey}}"
              },
              {
                "key": "X-Tenant-Id",
